+// b2390 WNM (owner: "We need to work on improving willow"; Deep: her heal is ready with no mate within 4 on 28.8% of her rounds v
+// 19.8% for the top 3). Runtime data flag WNM_TAB[1], read first; 0 = v904. Bit 1: while her heal cooldown <= 2, no living mate within 4,
+// no foe within 6 and she is not on her own running capture, her OWN row (wl2_pull, her sight) scales every group no mate claims and no
+// mate stands within 6 of by WNM_K / 1000: a group by a mate wins, and when no such group exists the order is live's (RC C1297: never a
+// refusal into idleness).
+#define WNM_BITS 0
+#define WNM_K 10
+inline const volatile int WNM_TAB[3] = { 0x574E4D31, WNM_BITS, WNM_K }; // slot 0 magic keeps it out of .bss
+#define WNM_ON(b) ((WNM_TAB[1] & (b)) != 0)
+// b2390 WSS (same task). Runtime data flag WSS_TAB[1], read first; 0 = v904. Bit 1: in the heal-first call, when her heal is ready and no
+// mate in heal reach is worth a heal (wl2_heal found none), a seen mate at heal reach + 1 .. WSS_FAR (not recalling, not on our spawn)
+// missing >= 3 x her Focus (a full heal, no overheal; RC C1342) draws one step toward it (before any camp attack), then the heal rule
+// runs again.
+#define WSS_BITS 0
+#define WSS_FAR 8
+inline const volatile int WSS_TAB[3] = { 0x57535331, WSS_BITS, WSS_FAR }; // slot 0 magic keeps it out of .bss
+#define WSS_ON(b) ((WSS_TAB[1] & (b)) != 0)
